    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d809">

                <pb facs="0755" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/2098a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Department of State to the Department of the
                        Navy</hi><anchor n="95" xml:id="d809-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-27">June 27, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Substance of Proposed Reply to
                        Admiral Hart</hi></p>
                <p>In view of your estimate that under present conditions your forces at Shanghai
                    are adequate, you are authorized, provided the American Consul at Shanghai
                    concurs and if, in the event that such a contingency arises, you are able to
                    work out a mutually satisfactory arrangement with the Japanese, to proceed in
                    such a contingency in accordance with your recommendation, that is, to arrange
                    that the American marines take over in Defense Sector B the functions now
                    allocated to British troops.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d809-f1" n="95" type="source" xml:id="d809-f1-content">
                <p>Approved by the Secretary of State and cabled by the Navy Department to Admiral
                    Hart after President Roosevelt had been consulted by the Chief of Naval
                    Operations (Stark).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
